    "title": "What channel is Michigan vs Saint Louis today? Time, TV for March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 12:14 p.m. ETEditor's note: Follow our live updates from Michigan vs. St. Louis in March Madness.Michigan basketball is taking on Saint Louis in the second round of the NCAA Tournament.The 1-seed Wolverines rolled 16-seed Howard after a slow start in the first half, beating the Bison 101-80 to earn a spot in the second round against Saint Louis.The Billikens, a 9-seed, had a more convincing victory over 8-seed Georgia in the first round, taking a 17-point lead at the half and then scored 53 more points in the second half for a dominant 102-77 win.Now, the two teams will square off in Buffalo, New York at KeyBank Center for the first game of the day, tipping off at 12:10 p.m. on CBS.Watch Michigan-SLU on Fubo (free trial)The 1-seed Wolverines are a Final Four favorite after finishing the regular season No. 3 in the USA TODAY Sports Coaches Poll.Michigan had arguably its best regular season ever comfortably winning the Big Ten regular season crown and then making it to the Big Ten Tournament title game before faltering against 7-seed Purdue (who enters the NCAA Tournament as a 2-seed).Now, with a tournament victory in the books, the Wolverines have turned their sights to Saint Louis.With a first-round win against the Bison, the Wolverines are looking to reestablish themselves as championship contenders after a loss in the conference tournament.Here's what you need to know about Michigan's second-round game:Michigan vs. Saint Louis March Madness game timeDate: Saturday, March 21.Time: 12:10 p.m.Location: KeyBank Center, Buffalo.Michigan basketball vs. Saint Louis TV channelTipoff: 12:10 p.m.Channel: CBS.Streaming: Fubo (free trial).Watch CBS NCAA Tournament games on Fubo (free trial)Where is Sweet 16, Elite Eight for Midwest region?Dates: March 27 & March 29.Location: United Center, Chicago.If the Wolverines advance to the Sweet 16 with a win over Saint Louis, they'll be heading back to Chicago, where they just went to the Big Ten Tournament final and lost to Purdue, where two wins can get them to the Final Four in Indianapolis.Need to catch up on the news during your lunch break? Sign up for our Sports Briefing newsletter to get daily summaries of Detroit sports! You can reach Christian at cromo@freepress.com.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
